From: Jeff Hagadorn <jeff@aletheia.io>
Subject: [PATCH] platform/x86: oxpec: add ONEXPLAYER X2Mini PRO

The ONEXPLAYER X2Mini PRO ships the same system board as the ONEXPLAYER
APEX, which is already handled as oxp_fly. The only thing that keeps the
driver from binding is the DMI board name, so add an entry pointing at
the same board type.

Verified on the unit:
  /sys/class/dmi/id/board_vendor -> ONE-NETBOOK
  /sys/class/dmi/id/board_name   -> ONEXPLAYER X2Mini PRO

Without this, `modprobe oxpec` fails with ENODEV and the machine has no
route to TDP control, fan control, or a battery charge limit.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Hagadorn <jeff@aletheia.io>
---
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/oxpec.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/oxpec.c
@@ -152,6 +152,13 @@
 	{
 		.matches = {
 			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_VENDOR, "ONE-NETBOOK"),
+			DMI_EXACT_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "ONEXPLAYER X2Mini PRO"),
+		},
+		.driver_data = (void *)oxp_fly,
+	},
+	{
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_VENDOR, "ONE-NETBOOK"),
 			DMI_EXACT_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "ONEXPLAYER APEX"),
 		},
 		.driver_data = (void *)oxp_fly,
